BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Step: 4) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (Title: Document the note like a lender would) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (Action: Draft principal, rate, accrual, schedule, balloon, default and cure terms, guarantee, collateral, setoff rights, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (subordination language.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (Detail: The note needs principal, interest start, payment schedule, balloon, default and cure provisions, guarantee,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (perfected collateral, and setoff limits [Escamilla Law Office - ZGklOUqHKYg @ 00:11:35]. Bank counsel will check) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (it for subordination and standby language before closing [Josh Kim - W3nhTnkKZcU @ 00:08:23].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (The equity-counting seller note runs on hard rules. Josh Kim separates two animals. A note counted toward the equity) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (injection must sit on full standby for the life of the loan. A note layered on top of a full 10% buyer injection can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (structured however you want, as long as three conditions hold: the bank stays in first position, the seller subordinates,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (and combined SBA plus seller payments still clear 1.25x debt service coverage [W3nhTnkKZcU @ 00:04:29]. Allan) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (Peterson is the SBA lender on JackQuisitions who closed over $70 million in acquisition financing last year. Peterson) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (adds the cap: the standby note cannot account for more than 50% of the required injection. That ends the old play of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (two years on standby followed by three years of principal-and-interest payments with no balloon [I6M8wAaqm5s @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (00:22:18]. Owner Actions spells out the floor. Buyer cash of 5% is now the minimum, reachable only with a 5% seller) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (note on full standby across a 10-year term. Sellers who never blinked at 24 months now treat 10 years as a sticking) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (point [lfjqb1es1E4 @ 00:00:16]. Peterson also stresses that the 10% is measured against total project cost, not just the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (purchase price. Total project cost includes bank-provided working capital and the line of credit Peterson always builds) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (in [I6M8wAaqm5s @ 00:24:02].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (The street tactics for selling a decade-long standby note are specific. Evan DiLeonardi's own first deal closed at 90/5/5,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (back when a 2-year standby still counted toward the down payment. DiLeonardi recommends stacking the note on top) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (of the price. If you want to offer $1 million, offer $1.05 million and ask for the extra $50,000 on full standby.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (Alternatively, offer $1,025,000 and split the difference as a sweetener [zBzv99U7MyE @ 00:02:17]. DiLeonardi adds) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (that some banks allow interest-only payments during the 10-year stint, so the seller still collects interest while principal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (waits, though that sits at the bank's discretion. Allan Peterson has watched buyers in the pipeline request a 5% note for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (the life of the loan, cite secondary market data showing it would be abnormal to hold the loan to maturity, and then) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (bump the offer by 5% [I6M8wAaqm5s @ 00:23:27]. Peterson's language tip: always say 'for the life of the loan,' never) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm ('10 years.' Then instill confidence that you will pay down early or refinance into conventional business banking once) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (you hold three years of business tax returns as owner [I6M8wAaqm5s @ 00:30:56]. Host Jack used the same play with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (a hyper-growth plan projecting a four-to-six-year payoff, and that seller got paid off significantly quicker) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm ([I6M8wAaqm5s @ 00:34:39].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (For notes outside the injection and for contingent money, the mechanics get creative. The SBA University instructor) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (splits large notes. A $500,000 note on a $1 million deal becomes two $250,000 notes. The first is greenlit for payments) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (from month one, so it becomes eligible for an SBA refinance after 24 months, at which point payments start on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (second [s5o1MBGuspY @ 00:06:43]. Keira Hamilton flags forgivable, performance-based note language: all or part of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.12 Tm (the note is forgiven if the buyer misses revenue, EBITDA, or customer retention targets within a set period) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.90 Tm ([7RAyVC1b9Pg @ 00:03:03]. Roland Frasier sizes earnout payouts with a simple Excel model. Take a business) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 145.67 Tm (clearing $4 million with roughly $2 million going to SBA debt service. Paying the seller $600,000 a year for 10 years) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 130.45 Tm (eats 30% of what is left. Paying $1 million a year hits 50% and leaves little room to wiggle if things go down) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 115.22 Tm ([onN8dTJIXAM @ 00:06:31]. Jason Paul Rogers skips the formal earnout and writes a sidebar consulting agreement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 100.00 Tm (instead, such as an extra $100,000 if a key client does over $1 million in sales during the first six months post close.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 84.77 Tm (Rogers says a formal earnout will not work inside an SBA deal, and the legal fees swamp a seven-figure transaction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 69.55 Tm ([7w05y7xLcNI @ 00:03:30].) Tj ET
