BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 484.00 Tm (Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 461.77 Tm (The most expensive failure is skipping the LOI. The Letters of Intent episode opens with a buyer who spent 3 weeks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 446.55 Tm (negotiating price verbally and paid for an $8,000 environmental report, only to watch the seller take a higher offer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 431.32 Tm (because there was no LOI and no exclusivity; an LOI would have cost them an afternoon [VuuLz-8NiYg @ 00:00:14].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 416.10 Tm (The same episode walks through a $3M business where nobody discussed the diligence period, financing contingency,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 400.87 Tm (or asset versus stock sale, while the seller turned down other bids assuming an exclusivity that never existed. Oberman) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 385.65 Tm (Law Firm, handling about 100-plus transactions a year, says skipping the LOI misaligns expectations and can burn) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 370.42 Tm (thousands of dollars in legal fees [6uqSoqOVnsg @ 00:04:52]. SMB Law Group explains why the sequence matters:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 355.20 Tm (the LOI locks exclusivity before QoE spend, purchase agreements run 40 to 70 pages, and brokers field about 600) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 339.97 Tm (inbound inquiries, so an unlocked buyer is one of hundreds [OIcTvUbSEgM @ 00:04:29]. Eric Pacifici also warns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 324.75 Tm (never to sign an APA with a deposit and inspection period without help. Even with a signed letter, Letters of Intent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 309.52 Tm (cautions that a refundable $100K deposit can tie the seller up with a non-buyer, which is why they require proof of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 294.30 Tm (funds.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 279.07 Tm (The number-one deal killer after signing is a quality-of-earnings miss. SMB Law Group cites $2M of EBITDA) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 263.85 Tm (becoming $1.6M post-QoE, and pairs it with structure traps: don't list the SBA debt amount, and model the seller note) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 248.62 Tm (across standby, interest-only, and balloon periods, because a 50% note with a 12-month balloon is a trap) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 233.40 Tm ([OIcTvUbSEgM @ 00:33:34]. Escamilla Law Office's Texas $5M hypothetical stacks every failure at once: a 90-day) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 218.17 Tm (exclusivity period, a $300K working-capital dispute, a seller-note mismatch, lender conflicts, a customer consent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 202.95 Tm (requirement, and broad indemnification [juS-FdGX2o0 @ 00:16:23]. Escamilla also warns that SBA lenders restrict) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 187.72 Tm (seller notes through subordination and payment limits, so a note negotiated without the bank collapses. Two offers both) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 172.50 Tm (priced at $5M carry very different risk: all cash versus $4M at close, a $500K seller note, and a $500K earnout over 2) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 157.27 Tm (years. Ellie on the SMB PE panel shows the forgivable-note downside in numbers: $3M of EBITDA at 5x is $15M,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 142.05 Tm (with $10M at close and $5M forgivable, and missing by $500K forgives $2.5M [PF2SOneLrJ0 @ 00:25:13]. The same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 126.82 Tm (panel says a buyer cannot pay the full purchase price at closing and must hold back something.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 111.60 Tm (Post-signing people risk is where economics quietly leak. On the SMB PE panel, a plumbing seller and their son started) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 96.37 Tm (competing after the sale, and a sale-based non-compete needs roughly $100K to $200K of consideration to stick;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 81.15 Tm (Dennis adds a $100,000 tenant-improvement bill from a landlord, with landlords demanding deposits and personal) Tj ET
