BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 429.77 Tm (The most expensive add-back failure is the last-mile retrade. growthink reports that the majority of the time, once the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 414.55 Tm (quality of earnings report lands with the buyer, there is pushback and an attempted haircut to add-backs or EBITDA,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 399.32 Tm (and that is exactly when deals blow up [UfQ-Ho_j61s @ 00:18:34]. The trap usually starts with categories sellers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 384.10 Tm (assume are one-time. In one growthink case, bad debts appeared on the P&L every single year, which already proved) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 368.87 Tm (they were not non-recurring and would struggle to survive as add-backs [UfQ-Ho_j61s @ 00:33:07]. The Finance Lab) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 353.65 Tm (applies the same logic to legal fees: one litigation settlement is legitimate, a pattern of recurring legal disputes is not,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 338.42 Tm (and the buyer should demand to see the invoice before crediting a dollar [hIU9zSg4cQg @ 00:00:20]. The economics) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 323.20 Tm (are brutal in both directions. At six times trailing EBITDA, $250,000 of accepted adjustments is worth $1.5 million of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 307.97 Tm (enterprise value if the seller gets full credit [UfQ-Ho_j61s @ 00:03:52]. That multiplier cuts both ways: every line a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 292.75 Tm (buyer strikes during diligence comes off the price at six times its face value, so a seller defending a weak add-back is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 277.52 Tm (defending value that was never really there.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 262.30 Tm (Working capital is where signed deals go to die after the handshake. Kirk Michie says nondisclosure agreements almost) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 247.07 Tm (never trigger lawsuits, but net working capital pegs and formulas generate lots and lots of post-purchase disputes, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 231.85 Tm (the letter of intent is a ceiling that only gets worse afterward [QqemANnN2ZM @ 00:03:07]. Transact Capital's Ross) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 216.62 Tm (Harris has watched deals die over working capital when sellers did not understand the process, with closings turning) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 201.40 Tm (contentious and deal threatening [YAk3dxgnsBU @ 00:12:43]. The post-close clock is unforgiving. A Simple Model) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 186.17 Tm (lays out the timeline: the buyer gets 60 to 120 days to deliver a closing statement, the seller gets roughly 30 days to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 170.95 Tm (review it, and any disagreement must be delivered in writing with reasonable detail before that window expires, while) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 155.72 Tm (escrowed funds stay frozen until both sides sign [C-seCQXqtM4 @ 00:02:18]. Break Into Finance flags the gaming) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 140.50 Tm (risk built into the mechanism itself: a seller who understands cyclicality can let the peg get set off a trough month and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 125.27 Tm (then close in a known peak month like January to harvest a big purchase price uplift [S31vo0Umk5M @ 00:24:20].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 110.05 Tm (Sellers who sleep through the review window and buyers who accept a trough-based peg both eat the loss.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 94.82 Tm (The final economics check is whether the cash actually shows up. John Colley has seen companies report $20 million) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 79.60 Tm (of EBITDA yet generate only $8 million of free cash flow, with $12 million vanishing into working capital,) Tj ET
