BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.97 Tm (valued as a claim, so neither a rep nor a note offset could recover it [LStVgWOM2LI @ 00:07:18]. The economics) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.75 Tm (check is identical in every case: a claim only has real value when money is already parked in escrow or a holdback, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.52 Tm (is still owed to the seller on a note you control.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.30 Tm (Tax surprises land late and wreck the agreed price. Josh Siegel warns that a silent LOI lets the buyer assume an asset) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 359.07 Tm (deal while the seller assumes a stock deal, and recalls a roughly $60M deal where the seller questioned the after-tax) Tj ET
